Worktree: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/182-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (your current directory).
Spec folder: specs/cli-external-orchestration/082-opencode-v1-v2-dual-compat/040-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (pre-approved, skip Gate 3)

ROLE: Act as a code agent. Fix two gaps in one function, `blankQuotedSpans` in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.mjs`, plus tests.

Problem:
1. ANSI-C quoting: in `$'it\'s --model p/m </dev/null'` a backslash escapes the next character, so `\'` does not end the span. The function ends the span at that `\'`, leaves ` --model p/m </dev/null` unblanked, and the stdin and model checks pass on prompt text.
2. A quoted heredoc delimiter is kept only when it matches `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`. Bash accepts any quoted word, so `<<'END-MARK'` is blanked to `<<''` and the stdin check wrongly fails a dispatch whose stdin is that heredoc.

Fix:
1. When `$'` opens a span, read to the matching `'` and skip the character after every backslash; blank the span to `''` (drop the `$` too or keep it, either is fine as long as no text inside survives). An unterminated `$'` is left as it is today for an unterminated `'`.
2. After `<<` or `<<-` and optional spaces, keep a quoted delimiter of any non-empty run of characters other than the quote and a newline: `'...'` or `"..."`.
Update the comment above the function so it stays accurate and short.

Tests: in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs`, at the end of the test named 'stdin and model checks ignore flags and redirects inside a quoted prompt', add:
  assert.equal(stdin(String.raw`opencode run $'it\'s --model p/m </dev/null'`), false);
  assert.equal(model(String.raw`opencode run $'it\'s --model p/m </dev/null'`), false);
  assert.equal(stdin(`opencode run -m p/m <<'END-MARK'\nprompt\nEND-MARK`), true);
  assert.equal(stdin(`opencode run -m p/m <<"END MARK"\nprompt\nEND MARK`), true);
Every other test must keep passing.

Comments keep the durable WHY and never name spec paths, phases, or task, review or finding ids.

VERIFICATION (run each from the worktree root with node from /Users/michelkerkmeester/.nvm/versions/node/v26.8.2/bin on PATH; all must pass):
node --check .skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.mjs
node --test .skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs

